nodecode-marketing is a rewrite of indranilbanerjee's indranilbanerjee/neels-plugins:

  https://github.com/indranilbanerjee/neels-plugins
  commit 76fe70cf73f57c27031913e493dabe6aeb7eb3c0
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Indranil Banerjee (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's whole product, its 207 skills — 164 in strategy, 22 in
content and 21 in social — as a library the model searches and reads instead of
a list of names in every prompt. The skill names are the ones each SKILL.md's
frontmatter gives; the prose of every skill, and of the markdown guides that sit
beside it inside its own folder, is carried unchanged under skills/. The Hermes
adapter (__init__.py walking three folders and calling ctx.register_skill once
per skill) is two nlk:define-contract declarations and two tools; the scan that
used to happen at startup happens once, on the first call, and is kept until the
cell stops.

Left out: the Python. 161 scripts under the three groups' scripts/ folders, the
optional dependencies they pin, the commands/, agents/, references/ and
templates/ folders at each group's top level, and the group-level
skills-index.json. The skills that name a script say so, and the cell's manual
says the prose is what it carries, so a step that needs a script is either done
by hand from the formula the skill gives or run from a copy of the original
plugin the person already has. Also left out: the Hermes manifest plugin.yaml
and BUNDLE-MANIFEST.json, which describe the bundle to Hermes rather than the
product to a person.

Each group folder of the original carries its own LICENSE as well: MIT,
Copyright (c) 2026 Digital Marketing Pro (strategy), (c) 2026 ContentForge
(content), (c) 2026 SocialForge (social). ContentForge's NOTICE.md records one
file it ships under CC BY-SA 4.0, config/humanization-patterns.json; that file
is a script's data, and this rewrite does not carry it.
